    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// n8n's Agent node accepts a maximum of 2 language models, so a deeper\n// fallback chain is built as a retry ladder. Each tier swaps the OpenRouter slot.\n// 16 Aug 2026: every id below was verified live against OpenRouter -- it exists,\n// it is :free (no paid model, per the free-tier rule), and it actually returned\n// a tool_call in a real request. The previous ladder had a PAID gemini tier plus\n// two dead ids (gemma-4-31b-it:free rate-limited 429, ling-3.0-flash:free is\n// 404 free-tier-discontinued), which is why all 4 tiers failed on live traffic.\nconst TIERS = [\n  { orModel: 'nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free',   groqModel: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile' },\n  { orModel: 'nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free',       groqModel: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile' },\n  { orModel: 'nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free',   groqModel: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile' },\n  { orModel: 'openai/gpt-oss-20b:free',                  groqModel: 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile' }\n];\nconst prev = $input.first().json;\nconst attempt = Number(prev.__attempt ?? -1) + 1;\nif (attempt >= TIERS.length) {\n  throw new Error('All ' + TIERS.length + ' model tiers failed. Tried: ' + TIERS.map(t=>t.orModel).join(', '));\n}\nreturn [{ json: { ...prev, __attempt: attempt, orModel: TIERS[attempt].orModel, groqModel: TIERS[attempt].groqModel } }];"
      },
      "id": "ladder-KI6P1Q",
      "name": "Model Ladder",
